// Shared kinds and purpose trees come from `std` and the imported `us` systems.
// The actual system laws stay in those imported source files; this keeps the
// project-specific income and business-cost meanings visible at their source.

purpose business-income : income
purpose design : business-income

/// What Lumen adds to each paycheck's retirement deferral: money into Sam's 401(k)
/// from the employer, a kind of contribution.
purpose match : contribution

/// What each mortgage payment sets aside with the lender for property tax and
/// insurance: a move between Sam's own accounts, not a cost until it is paid out.
/// (Not `escrow`: that is the account's name, and an account and a purpose may not share one.)
purpose escrow-deposit : transfer

kind sole-proprietorship : entity
  /// The business identity used to recognize owner allocations on spending.

purpose spending
  /// A cost allocated to a sole proprietorship, or paid by it, is deductible
  /// on Schedule C. A bill remains one flow; only the business share is counted.
  law business-costs
    on flow
    when owner.kind is sole-proprietorship
    count amount as schedule-c-expenses
